1
00:00:35,446 --> 00:00:36,640
I’ve met her now.

2
00:00:38,179 --> 00:00:39,600
Is she a goat or a sheep?

3
00:00:40,461 --> 00:00:40,920
(Maybe a goat?)

4
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,960
A goat? Or is she a sheep?

5
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:43,840
Is she a sheep or a goat?

6
00:00:43,909 --> 00:00:44,920
(It’s a sheep.)

7
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,050
Okay.

8
00:00:46,075 --> 00:00:47,680
(Take a seat first.)

9
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:49,160
*staggering*

10
00:00:51,727 --> 00:00:52,727
(Cut!)

11
00:00:59,356 --> 00:01:00,680
(Let’s eat, Emi!)

12
00:01:01,081 --> 00:01:02,081
(Good job!)

13
00:01:02,221 --> 00:01:03,221
Finished!
[IT’S FINISHED, EVERYONE]

14
00:01:04,421 --> 00:01:05,322
(Yes, for this scene.)

15
00:01:05,781 --> 00:01:06,680
(You may go home now.)

16
00:01:07,366 --> 00:01:08,567
Thank you!

17
00:01:08,592 --> 00:01:09,516
(So smooth)

18
00:01:09,811 --> 00:01:10,880
(You spent three hours doing makeup!)
[COME BACK HERE!!!]

19
00:01:11,291 --> 00:01:13,442
We’ve finished the first scene.

20
00:01:13,518 --> 00:01:14,920
(What did they have you do just now?)

21
00:01:14,987 --> 00:01:18,440
They had me kind of drift in space.
[DRIFTING IN SPACE]

22
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:20,867
I was being pulled back to the moon

23
00:01:21,423 --> 00:01:22,640
although I wanted to go to Earth

24
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:26,560
to look for some human angel living there.

25
00:01:27,184 --> 00:01:29,607
While I was drifting, I did everything I was told.

26
00:01:29,648 --> 00:01:31,920
And so I kept drifting and drifting.

27
00:01:33,773 --> 00:01:36,507
I’m talking nonsense right now, so please
watch the MV to find out instead.

28
00:01:38,901 --> 00:01:41,160
(There’s a shepherd.)

29
00:01:41,213 --> 00:01:42,228
(And there’s a sheep in the room.)

30
00:01:42,354 --> 00:01:43,955
-(And you’re…)
-We aren’t being frugal, are we?

31
00:01:44,017 --> 00:01:46,961
(Yeah. You’re the human who takes care of it.)

32
00:01:47,292 --> 00:01:48,149
(Understood?)

33
00:01:49,842 --> 00:01:51,000
-(Huh?)
-I understand!

34
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:53,741
-I was just joking!
-(Okay.)

35
00:02:01,693 --> 00:02:02,813
Is she a star?

36
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,200
(Yeah. It’s her first time as a star.)

37
00:02:04,283 --> 00:02:04,960
Really?

38
00:02:06,399 --> 00:02:08,985
Are you wearing a costume?

39
00:02:10,812 --> 00:02:11,920
What’s her name?

40
00:02:12,377 --> 00:02:13,150
(She doesn’t have one yet.)

41
00:02:13,225 --> 00:02:14,200
She doesn’t?

42
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:16,000
Can I name her then?

43
00:02:16,259 --> 00:02:17,040
(Alright.)

44
00:02:17,351 --> 00:02:18,160
How about “Elizabeth”?!

45
00:02:18,185 --> 00:02:19,280
(Who are you calling?)

46
00:02:19,353 --> 00:02:20,600
Do you want to be called “Elizabeth“?

47
00:02:21,165 --> 00:02:22,720
The name “Elizabeth” seems to suit her.

48
00:02:23,587 --> 00:02:24,400
Elizabeth!

49
00:02:25,469 --> 00:02:27,400
By the time I finish saying that name,
all your friends are already back in the pen.

50
00:02:28,156 --> 00:02:28,960
Let’s just call her “Alice”.

51
00:02:29,074 --> 00:02:30,013
(Good idea!)

52
00:02:30,038 --> 00:02:30,960
Alice!

53
00:02:31,089 --> 00:02:33,160
-(How about “Alice”?)
-(Are you calling me?)

54
00:02:33,811 --> 00:02:34,767
She’s just adorable. Very lovely.

55
00:02:34,792 --> 00:02:36,548
[SO ADORABLE]

56
00:02:37,039 --> 00:02:40,160
So I named her Elizabeth, or Alice in short.

57
00:02:41,431 --> 00:02:42,760
(Woah!)

58
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:45,360
(She has stayed calm for so long!)

59
00:02:45,454 --> 00:02:46,720
(Are you afraid of sheep, Bonnie?)

60
00:02:47,293 --> 00:02:48,125
I’m not.

61
00:02:48,153 --> 00:02:51,400
But what scared Alice just now
that made her rush to the camera?!

62
00:02:51,442 --> 00:02:52,760
(She was startled.)

63
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,414
Eh? Did she just poop? Eh?
[SHE JUST PLANTED A BOMB]

64
00:03:31,606 --> 00:03:33,520
Listen to me. She loves me!

65
00:03:33,716 --> 00:03:36,280
She jumped onto the bed just to see me!

66
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,352
(Have you ever sung with a sheep?)

67
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:52,589
Singing with a sheep?

68
00:03:52,614 --> 00:03:53,190
(Yeah!)

69
00:03:53,261 --> 00:03:54,960
This is my first time ever.

70
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:59,395
Elizabeth seems to be a bit startled,
so she’s taking a break now.

71
00:03:59,438 --> 00:04:01,704
(She also sang with you just now.)

72
00:04:01,821 --> 00:04:03,640
Baa! She really flowed with the melody.

73
00:04:05,274 --> 00:04:06,879
Baa! Baa!

74
00:04:06,964 --> 00:04:08,080
She was looking for her mother,

75
00:04:09,424 --> 00:04:10,486
who was right here.

76
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,552
(Will Alice sing the chorus of this song?)

77
00:04:12,584 --> 00:04:13,370
Alice as a chorus singer?

78
00:04:13,469 --> 00:04:15,600
She’ll be RISER MUSIC’s new star.

79
00:04:15,684 --> 00:04:17,481
(So are we rooting for her now?)

80
00:04:17,506 --> 00:04:19,048
Yeah, please stay tuned for her work!

81
00:04:19,257 --> 00:04:20,941
I named her myself.

82
00:04:21,073 --> 00:04:22,737
[SHE’S UNDER MY MANAGEMENT]
She’s an artist of Bonnie House.

83
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,600
(You have to take her out to events as well.)

84
00:04:24,625 --> 00:04:26,680
Oh, darn! Now I’m feeling bad for her.

85
00:04:26,771 --> 00:04:28,250
Let her go home and graze in peace.

86
00:04:28,289 --> 00:04:30,236
(She already ate some of the grass here.)

87
00:04:30,261 --> 00:04:31,828
She did, then she pooped right here.

88
00:04:33,508 --> 00:04:37,080
Then she went up to me and I thought
she loved me and wanted my attention.

89
00:04:37,157 --> 00:04:38,880
Then, when the song ended, she pooped.

90
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,364
(But she finished her job first!)

91
00:04:40,412 --> 00:04:41,612
She did indeed!

92
00:04:42,447 --> 00:04:44,160
She pooped only after the director said “cut”!

93
00:04:44,464 --> 00:04:45,208
Pellets of it.

94
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:46,320
(At least she knew when to poop.)

95
00:04:46,348 --> 00:04:47,271
She did.

96
00:04:47,362 --> 00:04:50,520
This is the scene where I sit alone
waiting for someone to return.

97
00:04:50,597 --> 00:04:52,517
(I see you have a key with you.)

98
00:04:52,551 --> 00:04:53,080
Yeah.

99
00:04:53,105 --> 00:04:56,560
She kissed my neck… my necklace, actually.

100
00:04:56,707 --> 00:05:00,498
I wondered who she was, but she was already
back in space. Already back to the Moon.

101
00:05:29,447 --> 00:05:30,720
Look into the camera!

102
00:05:32,769 --> 00:05:34,483
Oh, she wants her mother now.

103
00:06:07,603 --> 00:06:10,965
Hello! Today I’ll give you
a tour around the house.

104
00:06:11,044 --> 00:06:12,601
It’s where you have dreams.

105
00:06:13,297 --> 00:06:17,352
Where I have a dream of someone kissing me.

106
00:06:17,437 --> 00:06:19,000
P’Jack! This is how the story goes!

107
00:06:20,001 --> 00:06:20,961
Let me tell you the story!

108
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:24,372
This is my own house.

109
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:27,760
I sleep in the damaged part of it.

110
00:06:27,789 --> 00:06:31,920
Every night, in my dream, I see
a short-haired woman.

111
00:06:33,523 --> 00:06:37,047
She comes to me and kisses my necklace.

112
00:06:37,133 --> 00:06:38,480
[HER OWN STORY SPOOKS HER]
That’s scary!

113
00:06:38,701 --> 00:06:41,264
[LET ME CONTINUE FOR A BIT]
Still, in the dream, I feel like I love her.

114
00:06:41,304 --> 00:06:45,480
I wonder what I did to her in a past life to keep
dreaming about her like this, P’Jack.

115
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,081
(Did you take something out of its place?)

116
00:06:48,164 --> 00:06:50,574
I’m not sure if I’m being cursed.

117
00:06:50,756 --> 00:06:54,680
I picked up this necklace from the ground
outside the front entrance. Or is it… ?

118
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,800
(Is she trying to get it back?)

119
00:06:56,358 --> 00:06:58,038
Is she looking for it?

120
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,609
[LET’S CONTINUE WITH THE TOUR]

121
00:07:00,634 --> 00:07:02,831
This is the grass field for the sheep to graze.

122
00:07:02,861 --> 00:07:05,566
I have a sheep, and it needs grass.

123
00:07:05,613 --> 00:07:07,400
She also sleeps with you in your room.

124
00:07:07,553 --> 00:07:08,433
Yeah, she does.

125
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,760
She also poops and farts in the room.

126
00:07:10,899 --> 00:07:13,711
During the day, she enjoys a grass buffet here.

127
00:07:13,747 --> 00:07:15,840
The house has a vintage look.

128
00:07:15,885 --> 00:07:18,432
Although it’s a bit rundown

129
00:07:18,454 --> 00:07:21,128
it’s still habitable.

130
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,880
It’s a bit scary at night, though.

131
00:07:23,368 --> 00:07:24,360
(Is there electricity here?)

132
00:07:24,731 --> 00:07:25,191
Nope.

133
00:07:25,216 --> 00:07:25,765
We use candles.

134
00:07:25,855 --> 00:07:26,960
We use candles.

135
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:29,080
It’s no surprise if there’s something drifting

136
00:07:29,801 --> 00:07:31,360
all the way here from the moon.

137
00:07:31,923 --> 00:07:33,680
We’re now at the front door.

138
00:07:33,801 --> 00:07:36,960
Around us is Alice’s grass buffet area.

139
00:07:37,194 --> 00:07:38,273
This is the house’s entrance.

140
00:07:38,298 --> 00:07:39,400
Isn’t it beautiful?

141
00:07:40,034 --> 00:07:40,960
Let’s go!

142
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:43,248
Be careful! There’s a bit of mud here.

143
00:07:43,273 --> 00:07:45,640
It’s kind of a mud spa.
[A MUD SPA AT THE FRONT]

144
00:07:45,665 --> 00:07:46,640
(A mud spa.)

145
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:49,897
Now I meant for it to look this way.

146
00:07:50,030 --> 00:07:54,000
I hired a painter to pour cassia leaf curry

147
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,056
over the front porch steps.

148
00:07:56,090 --> 00:07:58,541
I left it for about two years before washing it off.

149
00:07:58,566 --> 00:07:59,600
That’s why the steps look like this.

150
00:07:59,656 --> 00:08:01,040
(Why did it have to be cassia leaf curry?)

151
00:08:01,065 --> 00:08:01,960
It’s for the green tone.

152
00:08:02,019 --> 00:08:05,240
I want the steps to match the field in color.

153
00:08:05,265 --> 00:08:07,440
The house is also painted green.

154
00:08:07,708 --> 00:08:08,770
I didn’t want a modern look in the first place.

155
00:08:08,795 --> 00:08:10,040
I wanted a vintage one.

156
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:11,560
It’s a ghostly-style house.

157
00:08:12,506 --> 00:08:13,400
(Ghostly?)

158
00:08:13,722 --> 00:08:14,597
Ghostly, yes.

159
00:08:14,622 --> 00:08:18,073
I hired an architect specifically for the design.

160
00:08:18,096 --> 00:08:19,400
That’s why it looks ghostly.

161
00:08:19,818 --> 00:08:22,018
It’s a bit rundown here and there
but that’s just how the style is.

162
00:08:22,899 --> 00:08:23,880
Let’s take a look inside.

163
00:08:24,452 --> 00:08:25,720
This is just like the game Ghost!

164
00:08:26,457 --> 00:08:27,843
I play this piano everyday.

165
00:08:27,921 --> 00:08:30,600
And P’Mi is in charge of the curtains.

166
00:08:30,951 --> 00:08:31,880
Am I?

167
00:08:32,162 --> 00:08:33,497
Yeah! Go, go!

168
00:08:33,614 --> 00:08:35,560
Oh, she’s the homeowner.

169
00:08:36,421 --> 00:08:37,528
This is the sofa.

170
00:08:37,553 --> 00:08:40,200
I live alone, so it’s for the ghosts as well.

171
00:08:40,309 --> 00:08:43,000
This is pretty scary. It’s getting dark now,
so I don’t want to say anything much.

172
00:08:43,264 --> 00:08:44,697
Look at the ceiling painting.

173
00:08:44,722 --> 00:08:45,360
There.

174
00:08:47,724 --> 00:08:49,988
I also keep the spiders here as pets.

175
00:08:50,013 --> 00:08:52,480
When a thief breaks in, they’ll cover
the entrance with their web, blocking passage.

176
00:08:52,505 --> 00:08:53,507
(It’s a ghostly-style house.)

177
00:08:53,563 --> 00:08:55,006
A ghostly-style house indeed.

178
00:08:55,049 --> 00:08:56,388
I keep a few spiders.

179
00:08:56,413 --> 00:08:57,239
(Only a few?)

180
00:08:57,264 --> 00:08:59,915
Only a few. But I think they have laid eggs
and had some hatchlings already.

181
00:08:59,936 --> 00:09:02,160
There’s one over there, already dead.

182
00:09:03,106 --> 00:09:04,280
This is getting spooky.

183
00:09:04,539 --> 00:09:05,507
Let’s get on with the shooting.

184
00:09:05,532 --> 00:09:06,320
(Okay!)

185
00:09:25,207 --> 00:09:26,807
(Smile only gently!)

186
00:09:28,758 --> 00:09:30,356
(Do a spin for me, P’Emi.)

187
00:09:30,381 --> 00:09:31,464
(Like when you danced.)

188
00:09:34,433 --> 00:09:35,433
(Like that!)

189
00:09:37,263 --> 00:09:38,360
(Keep doing that!)

190
00:09:47,541 --> 00:09:49,320
There’re tons of mosquitoes here, everyone!

191
00:09:49,394 --> 00:09:50,651
Bonnie is not okay!

192
00:09:51,726 --> 00:09:54,458
Cholly has never done anying like this before!

193
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:58,480
P’Mi does her scenes in a room
with a green screen and an air-conditioner,

194
00:09:58,505 --> 00:10:00,615
but Bonnie has to be out here and suffer.

195
00:10:00,698 --> 00:10:02,144
-(She’s from the sky, after all.)
-She’s from the sky?

196
00:10:02,174 --> 00:10:03,484
And I’m just an ordinary earthling?

197
00:10:03,793 --> 00:10:05,440
-That’s the fate of earthlings.
-(You’re bound to suffer.)

198
00:10:06,032 --> 00:10:06,920
It’s a fate full of hardships.

199
00:10:07,042 --> 00:10:08,360
I really want to wash my hair now.

200
00:10:08,779 --> 00:10:11,248
(Bon! Bon! Take off the head…)

201
00:10:11,273 --> 00:10:12,360
Are you calling me?

202
00:10:39,324 --> 00:10:40,160
Don’t look at it.

203
00:10:40,185 --> 00:10:41,320
What’s not seen doesn’t exist.

204
00:11:00,523 --> 00:11:01,960
(What’s the problem with this scene?)

205
00:11:02,444 --> 00:11:03,120
There’re lots of mosquitoes!

206
00:11:03,242 --> 00:11:04,439
(Lots of mosquitoes and other bugs, right?)

207
00:11:04,586 --> 00:11:06,712
It’s dark now, and it’s raining too.

208
00:11:07,289 --> 00:11:08,268
(And the ground is muddy.)

209
00:11:08,347 --> 00:11:10,391
The bugs are just… Eek!

210
00:11:11,205 --> 00:11:12,828
But the scene looks fantastic!

211
00:11:13,247 --> 00:11:14,880
(Can you explain what happens in the scene?)

212
00:11:16,691 --> 00:11:19,200
I’m about to fly out of here, but she grabs me.

213
00:11:19,338 --> 00:11:20,760
(Okay. Do you really want to go away?)

214
00:11:21,008 --> 00:11:24,327
I have to! If I don’t fly back today,
I won’t be able to come back to Earth again!

215
00:11:25,504 --> 00:11:26,640
Come back!

216
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:45,440
Is it okay?

217
00:11:46,069 --> 00:11:46,840
(Well done!)

218
00:11:46,932 --> 00:11:47,800
Is it okay?

219
00:11:47,856 --> 00:11:48,450
(Yeah!)

220
00:11:48,475 --> 00:11:49,600
Yay.
[WE’VE GOT THIS SCENE]

221
00:11:49,790 --> 00:11:52,400
(I’ll send you two to the medic!)

222
00:12:08,823 --> 00:12:10,200
(What happened just now?)

223
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:11,680
It’s raining.

224
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:14,680
Wet Look.

225
00:12:15,190 --> 00:12:16,646
But I don’t want to look that wet.

226
00:12:16,671 --> 00:12:17,880
We moved here to do some shooting
in the meantime.

227
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:19,200
The moon is over there.

228
00:12:19,576 --> 00:12:21,080
When the rain stops, we’ll shoot there later.

229
00:12:45,461 --> 00:12:47,960
(And three, two, one, action!)

230
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:49,640
(Turn around now!)

231
00:12:51,041 --> 00:12:52,080
(Then look up!)

232
00:12:53,712 --> 00:12:54,960
(And three…)

233
00:12:57,489 --> 00:12:58,760
(And cut!)

234
00:13:09,864 --> 00:13:11,283
(How many outfits have you worn today?)

235
00:13:11,308 --> 00:13:13,680
This is my second outfit.

236
00:13:13,711 --> 00:13:16,040
I’m about to sit on the moon now.

237
00:13:16,981 --> 00:13:19,400
Am I right? It’s a rock on the moon.

238
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:22,480
It’s our line sync scene. Last scene for today.

239
00:13:22,659 --> 00:13:23,335
(Really?)

240
00:13:25,157 --> 00:13:26,240
It’s the last one!

241
00:14:01,327 --> 00:14:02,687
Yay!

242
00:14:02,712 --> 00:14:04,560
It’s over!

243
00:14:05,997 --> 00:14:09,600
We’ve finished shooting the MV
for our new song, titled

244
00:14:09,659 --> 00:14:11,920
MOON KEY!

245
00:14:13,792 --> 00:14:14,628
Yay!

246
00:14:14,653 --> 00:14:15,653
MOON KEY!

247
00:14:15,857 --> 00:14:17,520
MOON KEY!

248
00:14:17,545 --> 00:14:19,880
(What’s your favourite scene?)

249
00:14:19,979 --> 00:14:20,960
The one where I play with Elizabeth, of course!

250
00:14:21,015 --> 00:14:22,615
Well, will she know?

251
00:14:22,733 --> 00:14:23,779
She will! I told her at the beginning!

252
00:14:23,804 --> 00:14:25,618
Oh, you told her already?
I named her myself when we first met!

253
00:14:25,669 --> 00:14:27,673
She’s under your management?

254
00:14:27,768 --> 00:14:30,320
She’s my pet. Her name is Elizabeth.

255
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:32,000
-Lovely.
-Her nickname is Alice.

256
00:14:32,119 --> 00:14:34,339
I didn’t get to play a single scene with her.

257
00:14:34,410 --> 00:14:35,498
She’s so adorable!

258
00:14:35,554 --> 00:14:39,320
When the director told her to get on the bed,

259
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,840
she jumped right up beside me.

260
00:14:40,901 --> 00:14:41,901
Whoa!

261
00:14:43,698 --> 00:14:44,838
-She’s friendly, isn’t she?
-(She is.)

262
00:14:44,896 --> 00:14:46,840
And what did she do after she jumped?

263
00:14:46,890 --> 00:14:48,320
She stayed with me till the end!

264
00:14:48,390 --> 00:14:49,650
Till the end.

265
00:14:50,024 --> 00:14:50,916
And what did she do next?

266
00:14:50,941 --> 00:14:51,612
She pooped.

267
00:14:51,637 --> 00:14:54,437
She pooped as if to say goodbye to Bonnie.

268
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,560
She pooped right there.

269
00:14:55,590 --> 00:14:59,628
-They were like tapioca balls.
-That marks the end of the scene.

270
00:14:59,653 --> 00:15:01,810
She left us so many pellets.

271
00:15:01,835 --> 00:15:02,760
She eats a lot, after all.

272
00:15:03,454 --> 00:15:05,407
She ate the grass in the scene.

273
00:15:05,474 --> 00:15:08,136
It was real grass, because she ate it.
[SHE REALLY GRAZED AND POOPED]

274
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:13,000
She really grazed and she really pooped.

275
00:15:13,556 --> 00:15:18,560
Okay, my favourite scene is my first CG scene.

276
00:15:18,907 --> 00:15:21,400
The one where you fly?

277
00:15:21,834 --> 00:15:24,920
The one with the blue screen where I fly
while trying to reach for Bonnie.

278
00:15:25,031 --> 00:15:26,440
Then my body starts to glow before exploding.

279
00:15:27,034 --> 00:15:28,634
(In your imagination, you were flying?)

280
00:15:28,673 --> 00:15:31,172
-(But in reality…)
-In reality, I was just standing on my toes.

281
00:15:31,198 --> 00:15:33,240
But they’ll make it look like I’m really flying,

282
00:15:33,318 --> 00:15:35,400
as if I’m riding a horse.
[SEE IT FOR YOURSELF IN THE MV]

283
00:15:35,483 --> 00:15:36,844
Have you met Elizabeth?

284
00:15:37,189 --> 00:15:41,153
-I have, but we had no scene together.
-She cried “Baa! Baa!”

285
00:15:41,281 --> 00:15:43,080
Yeah! She cried like that

286
00:15:43,217 --> 00:15:46,873
-since eight in the morning!
-She cried along with the melody!

287
00:15:46,898 --> 00:15:48,133
♪ There may be nights ♪

288
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:48,748
Baa!

289
00:15:48,779 --> 00:15:50,580
♪ When there’s no moon in the sky ♪

290
00:15:50,605 --> 00:15:51,120
Baa!

291
00:15:51,145 --> 00:15:51,673
Like this!

292
00:15:51,698 --> 00:15:52,933
Really? How adorable!

293
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:53,995
She really did it!
[SHE SANG THE CHORUS]

294
00:15:54,034 --> 00:15:55,178
(We’ll keep her cries in the mastered version.)

295
00:15:55,229 --> 00:15:57,342
I’ll look forward to it when I watch the BTS clip.

296
00:15:57,367 --> 00:15:59,920
If I don’t hear it, you’ll be in trouble, Elizabeth!

297
00:16:00,029 --> 00:16:03,160
Seeya! Please listen to the song MOON KEY.

298
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,077
Where will it be released?

299
00:16:04,111 --> 00:16:05,880
RISER MUSIC, all platforms!

300
00:16:06,066 --> 00:16:07,958
RISER MUSIC, all platforms!

301
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:09,240
You may enjoy it

302
00:16:09,309 --> 00:16:10,960
on all music streaming platforms!

303
00:16:12,643 --> 00:16:14,080
-(Bye-bye!)
-Bye-bye!

